From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: let web apps use the files of web app modules

Web apps of one kind share user scripts, such as the HbbTV terminal
that broadcasters' apps run on, and each app had to ship its own copy.
A new add-on type, kodi.webapp.module, holds such files: a web app
imports the module and names a file of it in its manifest as
<userscript addon="module id">path</userscript>, and likewise in a
<contentfilter>, so the app keeps the order of its scripts. Modules are
hidden like other add-on libraries.

The client knows a module's file as "<module id>.<file name>", so files
of the app and of its modules never replace one another in the client,
which keys content filters by name. The web player refuses to open an
app that names a file of an add-on it does not import, a file that does
not exist, one whose name the client rejects, or two content filters of
one name.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
